   "script_line": "Two operational demands the beach makes and the farm does not. The first is time. On the beach people get hungry at unpredictable hours and have short patience under the sun. A wait time communicated — “it is twenty minutes, shall I bring you water meanwhile?” — settles ninety per cent of complaints before they exist. What generates a complaint is not waiting; it is waiting without information. The second is sun and water. Shade, cold water, toilets checked hourly, attention to children and older people at midday. Wellbeing on the beach is mostly reducing physical discomfort nobody puts into words.",
